# What the image build must not take from the checkout it runs in. The build
# installs its own node_modules with npm ci and makes its own dist; a copy from
# a developer's machine (another OS's native binaries, an old build, a stale
# TypeScript build record) would land on top of them. Local .env files are left
# out too: the bundle is built from the commit, nothing else.
node_modules
dist
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
npm-debug.log*
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
